    "result_text": "The build passes green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nA derived `riskFlag` boolean on the owner read model, true when any of the three signals hold:\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2014 `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()` (already stored at create time).\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email** \u2014 the email domain shares a base label with a known disposable-mail provider (`mailinator`, `tempmail`, `guerrillamail`), catching near-misses like subdomains/alternate TLDs that slip past the hard `DisposableEmailValidation` blocklist.\n3. **Over soft capacity** \u2014 `owner.getCapacityWarning()`, which is set when the city held \u226540 (the soft threshold, below the hard cap of 50).\n\n## Files touched (3) \u2014 kept structurally minimal\n\n- **`mapper/RiskFlags.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, cohesive helper mirroring the existing `OwnerSegments` pattern. All the new behaviour lives here, in a class whose `WMC_other` is near zero, so no existing large class grows.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `RiskFlags.of(owner)`, exactly like the surrounding expression mappings.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 one added `riskFlag` read-only boolean property on the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto`).\n\nI deliberately avoided adding a method to the large `Owner` model class, which would have paid the whole class's summed complexity as `WMC_other`. `RiskFlags.of` has CC 3 and the class carries almost no surrounding context, keeping every changed function simple.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` passes (a fully unique structured owner with no email returns `riskFlag: false`), and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
